@startuml 13_sequence_failure_recovery
!include ../style.iuml
title Sequence diagram: failure and recovery of a dossier in the pipeline
autonumber
skinparam maxMessageSize 230

participant "Intake" as IN
queue "Broker\n(Redis)" as BR
participant "Relay\nsweep" as RL
participant "Task\n(Celery)" as TK
database "Store\n(MongoDB)" as DB
participant "Dispatcher" as DI
participant "Reconciler" as RC
actor "Reviewer" as RV
actor "Operator\n(level 4)" as OP

== A. The broker is down ==
IN -> DB : write dossier + outbox marker (one atomic write)
note right of IN
  Intake never talks to the broker, so a broker
  outage cannot lose or block a submission.
end note
RL -> DB : every 10 s: list the markers still pending
RL -> BR : publish(claim_id, version, hash)
alt broker reachable
  BR --> RL : accepted
  RL -> DB : clear the marker
else broker down
  RL -x BR : publish fails
  RL -> RL : marker kept for the next sweep\n(counted as failed; "stale" once older than 60 s)
end

== B. A task fails ==
BR -> TK : process_claim(id, version, hash)
TK -x DB : error (store, model code, bug)
loop up to 3 retries
  TK -> TK : wait: random time between 0 and min(30 s, 1 s * 2^attempt)
  TK -> DB : try again
end
alt a retry succeeds
  TK -> DB : continues the pipeline up to "ready"
else retries exhausted
  TK -> DB : write a dead letter (reason = error type only,\nnever the message: it could quote claim text)
  TK -> DB : active state -> dead_lettered
end
OP -> DB : deadletters (list)
OP -> DB : deadletter-replay(dead_id)
DB --> OP : dead_lettered -> triaged, marker re-armed,\ndead letter removed (works once; otherwise conflict)

== C. A reviewer disappears ==
DI -> DB : every 60 s: leases past their end
DI -> DB : leased -> ready (reviewer avoided for that dossier if possible)
DI -> DI : also takes back dossiers held by someone who may\nno longer decide them (demoted, deactivated)
RV -> DB : decide after the lease ended
DB --> RV : refused (409 lease_lost), nothing written

== D. Periodic audit of the queue (every 5 minutes) ==
RC -> DB : check states, markers, counts, leases
alt expired lease found
  RC -> DB : repair: hand it back (the only automatic repair)
else anything else (stuck state, unpublished marker,\ntwo live leases, count mismatch, decided without a person)
  RC -> OP : reported for a person to look at, never guessed at
end
@enduml
